# Raw profiler output IS committed, under results/<run>/raw/ (docs/02_protocol.md §3.5, §6):
# .nsys-rep, .ncu-rep, .sqlite, SASS/PTX dumps, .cubin, tegrastats logs, torch.profiler traces, full CSV exports.
# Nothing below may match them. Never committed: model weights, datasets, caches, environments, secrets.

# model weights and checkpoints
checkpoints/
weights/
models/
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.npz
*.onnx
*.engine
*.gguf

# datasets
datasets/
*.hdf5
*.parquet

# caches and scratch space (Inductor / Triton caches, temporary profiler output before compression)
scratch/
.cache/
hf_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# credentials and tokens
.env
.netrc
.git-credentials
hf_token*
*.token
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# logs are ignored everywhere except inside a result directory
*.log
!results/**/*.log

# the fixture observation (PNG + JSON, possibly a small .npz) is allowed
!bench/fixtures/**

# research-side agent files, local to the server

# --- EXCEPTION to the "commit the raw data" rule above, added in T010 ---------------
# nsys binary reports embed SYSTEM-WIDE process metadata, including the environment of
# processes nsys did not launch. On this machine that includes a session token belonging to
# the agent's own harness, so every .nsys-rep and its .sqlite fails the protocol §3.5 secrets
# scan. Scrubbing the profiled process's environment does NOT remove it — verified by
# capturing under `env -i`, which still embeds it — so the binaries cannot be committed.
# They are kept on disk, listed in meta.json.raw_files with committed:false, the reason and
# the command that regenerates them, exactly as §3.5 prescribes. The exported CSVs under
# results/*/nsys/ carry the same measurements, are scanned clean, and ARE committed.
# .ncu-rep files are unaffected and are still committed (compressed).
results/**/*.nsys-rep
results/**/*.sqlite

# Overnight C1 attempt (2026-09-22): four .ncu-rep of 88-203 MB, produced by
# `--set full -c 300`. GitHub hard-rejects >100 MB and protocol §6 caps a committed file
# at 50 MB, so these cannot be committed as they are. They are superseded by the
# 2026-09-23 C1 captures (four targeted sections, ~900 KB compressed each). Kept on disk
# as raw evidence; listed committed:false.
results/20260922_E4g_pi0_ncu_eager/ncu/*.ncu-rep

# Local Claude Code settings (machine-specific permissions, not part of the study)
.claude/settings.local.json
